From 3b1f3ef1be51031802a5d317a43de54cf214bee5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 01:55:46 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 25/25] arm64: run x86-64 userspace through Darwin gadgets

Keep the UML kernel and kernel-mode execution arm64 while allowing the 4 KiB Darwin profile to load EM_X86_64 tasks. Tag those tasks in existing bridge padding and overlay their integer, TLS, and x87/SSE/AVX state on otherwise-unused arm64 register slots.

Route tagged tasks to the data-only gadgets engine, translate compatible native and long-mode INT 0x80 syscalls, and construct native x86-64 signal and XSAVE frames. Restore userspace edits to those frames through rt_sigreturn.

Leave the shared host/kernel ABI, the 16 KiB profile, Android, and non-Darwin builds unchanged. Syscalls whose compat argument layouts require explicit adapters remain rejected.
